rces, Apr 2022]","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q8N6H7","text":"GTPase-activating protein (GAP) for ADP ribosylation factor 1 (ARF1), which is essential for COPI vesicle formation and retrograde transport between the Golgi and the endoplasmic reticulum (PubMed:17760859, PubMed:20858901). Hydrolysis of ARF1-bound GTP leads to dissociation of coatomer from Golgi-derived membranes to allow fusion with target membranes (PubMed:20858901). Promotes the proper assembly of the COPI coat lattice, rather than just acting as a simple curvature-dependent GAP like ARFGAP1 (PubMed:20858901). Also acts as a regulator of STING1 activity, both by promoting cytokine secretion in certain cell types and promoting the proton channel activity of STING1 in the trans-Golgi (PubMed:39947179)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_03","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}